From: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
Date: Sun, 03 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] amdgpu/uapi,object: add PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR GEM create flag

Patch 1 added a lazy eviction path in amdgpu_dma_buf_map() so that a
VRAM BO is automatically moved to GTT when the GPU lacks large BAR and
an importer tries to DMA-map it.  That eviction happens at the point the
DMA-BUF is first mapped by an NVMe (or similar) device — meaning the BO
has already been allocated in VRAM and must be copied to GTT before the
first transfer can begin.  On busy systems this serializes the very first
transfer and briefly doubles the memory footprint.

Introduce AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR (bit 16 of the GEM
create flags) to let callers declare upfront that a BO will be used for
DMA-BUF P2P I/O on a system that may lack resizable BAR.  When the flag
is set and visible_vram_size < real_vram_size, amdgpu_bo_placement_from_
domain() redirects the effective placement from VRAM to GTT before the
placement-building loop runs.  The BO is therefore allocated in GTT from
the outset; no eviction is needed at DMA-BUF map_attachment time.

On large-BAR systems (visible_vram_size == real_vram_size) the flag is
silently ignored and the normal VRAM placement policy applies.

Intended users:
  * The ROCm / HIP runtime, which can set this flag when allocating device
    memory buffers the application will use as io_uring DMA-BUF targets
    (the "hipfile" use-case).
  * Direct users of the amdgpu GEM ioctls, such as the test program in
    userspace/amdgpu-dmabuf-io/, that want deterministic up-front placement
    rather than relying on the lazy eviction fallback introduced by patch 1.

Bit 16 is chosen to avoid collisions with current upstream flags (bits
0-11) and typical out-of-tree additions.

Signed-off-by: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
---
 amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c    | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 include/uapi/drm/amdgpu_drm.h | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/uapi/drm/amdgpu_drm.h b/include/uapi/drm/amdgpu_drm.h
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/include/uapi/drm/amdgpu_drm.h
+++ b/include/uapi/drm/amdgpu_drm.h
@@ -168,6 +168,23 @@
  */
 #define AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_GFX12_DCC			(1 << 11)
 
+/**
+ * AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR - prefer GTT placement on
+ * systems without resizable BAR (large BAR / ReBAR).
+ *
+ * On GPUs without resizable BAR only a portion of VRAM is exposed through
+ * the PCIe aperture.  Buffers intended for DMA-BUF peer-to-peer I/O (e.g.
+ * the io_uring hipfile path with NVMe) must reside in a region reachable by
+ * the importer's DMA engine.
+ *
+ * When this flag is set and visible_vram_size < real_vram_size, the driver
+ * places the BO in GTT instead of VRAM, avoiding an eviction at DMA-BUF
+ * map_attachment time.  On large-BAR systems the flag has no effect and the
+ * normal VRAM placement policy is used.
+ *
+ * Bit 16 is chosen to avoid collisions with existing upstream flags (0-11)
+ * and typical out-of-tree additions.
+ */
+#define AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR	(1 << 16)
+
 /* va regions */
 #define AMDGPU_VA_RANGE_32_BIT			0x1
 #define AMDGPU_VA_RANGE_HIGH			0x2
diff --git a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_object.c
@@ -138,6 +138,26 @@
 void amdgpu_bo_placement_from_domain(struct amdgpu_bo *abo, u32 domain)
 {
 	struct amdgpu_device *adev = amdgpu_ttm_adev(abo->tbo.bdev);
 	struct ttm_placement *placement = &abo->placement;
 	struct ttm_place *places = abo->placements;
 	u32 c = 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR: when the caller has
+	 * flagged this BO as a DMA-BUF P2P candidate and the GPU lacks large
+	 * BAR (visible VRAM < real VRAM), redirect the placement from VRAM to
+	 * GTT so the BO lands in system RAM from the outset.  No eviction is
+	 * then required when an importer calls dma_buf_map_attachment().
+	 *
+	 * On large-BAR systems real_vram_size == visible_vram_size so this
+	 * condition is never true and the flag has no effect.
+	 */
+	if ((abo->flags & AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_PREFER_GTT_NO_LARGE_BAR) &&
+	    (domain & AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM) &&
+	    adev->gmc.real_vram_size > adev->gmc.visible_vram_size) {
+		domain &= ~AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM;
+		domain |=  AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_GTT;
+	}
+
 	if (domain & AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_VRAM) {
